{"query":"Maharashtra Housing and Area Development Authority  official site amenities","follow_up_questions":null,"answer":null,"images":[],"results":[{"url":"https://www.mhada.gov.in/en/mumbai-board/lottery?q=Conveyance_contacts&page=38","title":"Maharashtra Housing and Area Development Authority - MHADA","content":"Providing proper amenities and maintenance of common infrastructural ... This is official website of Maharashtra Housing and Area Development Authority.","score":0.83452857,"raw_content":null,"id":"2f86c9-00"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maharashtra_Housing_and_Area_Development_Authority","title":"Maharashtra Housing and Area Development Authority - Wikipedia","content":"Maharashtra Housing and Area Development Authority\n\n| Official Seal of MHADA |\n| Agency overview |\n| Formed | 1977 |\n| Jurisdiction | Maharashtra |\n| Headquarters |  Bandra East, Mumbai, Maharashtra |\n| Agency executive |  Sanjeev Jaiswal, Vice President & Chief Executive Officer |\n| Parent agency | Ministry of Housing (Maharashtra) \"Ministry of Housing (Maharashtra)\") |\n| Website |  | [...] and local authorities for the construction of houses. The Bombay Building Repairs and Reconstruction Board was constituted in 1971. It was created to deal with the problems faced by tenants residing in dilapidated buildings in the Island City of Bombay and undertook its structural repairs and reconstruction to make them structurally sound and safe for habitation. The Bombay Slum Improvement Board was constituted in 1974, with intention to provide basic amenities, such as water taps, drainage, pathways, latrines and streetlights etc. in Bombay slums. To begin with, its activities were confined to the Mumbai City and Mumbai Suburban Districts. These activities were later extended to the remainder of Maharashtra upon the launch of the Maharashtra Housing & Area Development Authority (MHADA), [...] Rural Development  Sanitation \"Ministry of Sanitation (Maharashtra)\")  School Education \"Ministry of School Education (Maharashtra)\")  Skill Development and Entrepreneurship \"Ministry of Skill Development and Entrepreneurship (Maharashtra)\")  Social Justice \"Ministry of Social Justice (Maharashtra)\")  Socially and Educationally Backward Classes \"Ministry of Socially and Educationally Backward Classes (Maharashtra)\")  Soil and Water Conservation \"Ministry of Soil and Water Conservation (Maharashtra)\")  Special Assistance \"Ministry of Special Assistance (Maharashtra)\")  Special Backward Classes Welfare \"Ministry of Special Backward Classes Welfare (Maharashtra)\")  Sports and Youth Welfare \"Ministry of Sports and Youth Welfare (Maharashtra)\")  State Excise \"Ministry of State Excise","score":0.73778254,"raw_content":null,"id":"4b3e84-01"},{"url":"https://www.rprealtyplus.com/news-views/first-time-mhada-housing-offers-amenities-similar-to-private-developers-109263.html","title":"First Time MHADA Housing Offers Amenities Similar to Private ...","content":"Along with this, all new MHADA projects will include solar panels and parking for electric vehicles (EV). These amenities are being offered to","score":0.6847074,"raw_content":null,"id":"db36f5-02"},{"url":"https://www.99acres.com/mhada-layout-facilities-sector-8-charkop-mumbai-andheri-dahisar-npxid-r295729","title":"MHADA Layout Amenities - Sector 8 Charkop - 99acres.com","content":"Living at MHADA Layout in Sector 8 Charkop, Western Mumbai comes with active amenities such as car parking. All are operational and resident-ready. Is car","score":0.65676886,"raw_content":null,"id":"b4c55c-03"},{"url":"https://www.bajajfinserv.in/maharashtra-housing-and-area-development-authority","title":"MHADA Guide 2026: Lottery, Eligibility, Application and Housing Schemes","content":"## \n\n## MHADA vs. Private developers\n\n| Parameter | MHADA Housing | Private Developers |\n --- \n| Pricing | Highly Subsidized (30–50% lower) | Market-driven (Expensive) |\n| Possession time | Can be delayed (3–5 years) | Variable (RERA-bound) |\n| Legal security | 100% Clear Title & Gov. Backed | Risk of litigation/disputes |\n| Amenities | Basic (Garden, Lift, Security) | High-end (Pool, Gym, Clubhouse) |\n| Quality | Reliable / Standard | Premium to Luxury |\n\n## \n\n## Benefits of buying a MHADA Home\n\nHousing projects developed by the Maharashtra Housing and Area Development Authority (MHADA) provide numerous benefits for individuals seeking affordable and secure homeownership opportunities.\n\nMajor advantages of MHADA housing: [...] ## Understanding MHADA\n\nThe Maharashtra Housing and Area Development Authority (MHADA) is one of India's leading public housing authorities, dedicated to providing affordable and quality housing across Maharashtra. Its journey began in 1948 with the establishment of the Bombay Housing Board and later evolved into MHADA in 1977 under the Maharashtra Housing and Area Development Act.\n\nEstablished with the vision of \"Housing for All,\" MHADA was created to address the growing demand for organised, affordable, and sustainable housing. Today, the Maharashtra Housing and Area Development Authority plays a vital role in developing residential projects, conducting transparent housing lotteries, and supporting urban redevelopment initiatives across the state. [...] The Maharashtra Housing and Area Development Authority (MHADA) is a government housing authority that provides affordable homes through transparent lottery-based schemes across Maharashtra. From Mumbai and Pune to Thane and Nashik, MHADA helps eligible applicants access budget-friendly housing with clear titles, planned infrastructure, and simplified online application processes. Whether you are a first-time homebuyer or an investor, MHADA offers a reliable pathway to homeownership.\n\n## Understanding MHADA","score":0.6549173,"raw_content":null,"id":"8cbcfb-04"},{"url":"http://www.mhada.gov.in/en/history","title":"History - MHADA","content":"To provide basic amenities such as potabl